re readings up to **158/98**, and kidney markers that have worsened over time in the record. Your DNA/genomics also suggest higher predisposition to **hypertension and CKD progression**, but that does **not** by itself explain why you feel more exhausted now. What is new from you today is **progressive exhaustion over the last few months**, which needs to be matched against timing, severity, sleep, exertional tolerance, and any associated symptoms.\n\n**Preliminary interpretation**\nAt this stage, your fatigue could fit several possibilities. The more supported broad categories are: **sleep-related or lifestyle causes**, **blood-pressure/medication-related issues**, **kidney-related progression or metabolic causes**, and other common medical causes of fatigue such as **anemia, thyroid issues, infection/inflammation, or low mood/stress-related strain**. I do not yet have enough detail to rank these confidently. If you are also having **chest pain, fainting, severe shortness of breath, new leg swelling, black stools, or rapidly worsening weakness**, say that immediately because those would change the urgency.\n\n**Recommended questions**\nBy answering a few targeted questions, we can narrow this down more safely and accurately.\n\n**(1/4)** When did the exhaustion first start, and is it constant every day or does it come in waves?","textSignature":"{\"v\":1,\"id\":\"msg_087676d5cc032cdf0169da118fafe48191a333b7e0e521e3cb\",\"phase\":\"final_answer\"}"}],"api":"openai-codex-responses","provider":"openai-codex","model":"gpt-5.4","usage":{"input":19756,"output":396,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":20152,"cost":{"input":0.04939,"output":0.00594,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.055330000000000004}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1775899020662}}
